# Article 5 – Commercial Rights

All Commercial Rights are reserved exclusively by the Licensor.

Commercial use is prohibited unless expressly authorized under a separate Commercial License Agreement.

Any person or organization wishing to commercially use the Software must first obtain written authorization from the Licensor.

---

# Article 6 – Commercial Licensing

Commercial Licenses may be issued solely at the discretion of the Licensor.

Commercial Licenses may include, but are not limited to:

* Royalty-based agreements
* Monthly subscriptions
* Annual subscriptions
* Per-user licensing
* Enterprise licensing
* Lifetime licensing
* Custom licensing agreements

The pricing structure, duration, and scope of any Commercial License shall be determined solely by the Licensor.

The Licensor reserves the unrestricted right to approve or refuse any Commercial License request without obligation to provide a reason.

---

# Article 7 – Written Authorization Requirement

No Commercial Rights are granted unless the Licensee possesses a valid written Commercial License Agreement expressly authorized by the Licensor.

Emails discussing possible licensing, verbal discussions, invoices, quotations, negotiations, purchase orders, or assumptions shall not constitute permission.

Only a written Commercial License Agreement issued or expressly authorized by the Licensor grants Commercial Rights.

Absent such written authorization, all Commercial Use is unauthorized.

---

# Article 8 – Commercial Evaluation

Commercial organizations may evaluate the Software internally for up to **30 calendar days** solely for the purpose of deciding whether to obtain a Commercial License.

During evaluation they shall not:

* deploy the Software into production,
* generate revenue using the Software,
* provide services using the Software,
* redistribute the Software,
* sublicense the Software,
* make the Software available to third parties.

Continued use after the evaluation period requires a Commercial License.

---

# Article 9 – Restrictions

Without prior written authorization from the Licensor, no person or organization may:

* Sell the Software
* Redistribute the Software for commercial purposes
* Offer the Software as SaaS
* Embed the Software into commercial products
* White-label the Software
* Remove copyright notices
* Remove attribution
* Claim ownership
* Misrepresent authorship
* Circumvent the commercial licensing requirements

---

# Article 10 – Redistribution

Redistributions permitted under this License must:

* retain this License,
* retain copyright notices,
* identify significant modifications,
* preserve attribution to the Licensor.

Redistribution shall not grant Commercial Rights to recipients.

